        "listen": {
          "explanationKey": "Who was the United States’ main rival during the Cold War?",
          "facts": [
            "After World War II, the United States and the Soviet Union became rivals. This was called the Cold War.",
            "The United States was worried about communism spreading to other countries.",
            "Both countries had nuclear weapons, so people also feared a nuclear war."
          ],
          "newWords": [
            {
              "word": "rival",
              "meaning": "someone you compete against"
